"body": "{\"parse\":{\"title\":\"Lek (river)\",\"pageid\":236578,\"redirects\":[],\"wikitext\":\"{{Infobox river\\n| name                = Lek\\n| native_name         = \\n| name_native_lang    = \\n| other_name          = \\n| etymology           = \\n<!---------------------- IMAGE & MAP -->\\n| image               = Lek.Nieuwegein.jpg\\n| image_size          = 220\\n| image_caption       = The Lek River near [[Nieuwegein]].\\n| map                 = Location Lek.PNG\\n| map_size            = 220\\n| map_caption         = Location of Lek in dark blue.\\n| pushpin_map         = \\n| pushpin_map_size    = 220\\n| pushpin_caption     = \\n<!---------------------- LOCATION -->\\n| subdivision_type1   = Country\\n| subdivision_name1   = [[Netherlands]]\\n| subdivision_type2   = \\n| subdivision_name2   = \\n| subdivision_type3   = Region\\n| subdivision_name3   = [[Utrecht (province)|Utrecht]], [[South Holland]]\\n| subdivision_type4   = \\n| subdivision_name4   = \\n| subdivision_type5   = \\n| subdivision_name5   = \\n<!---------------------- PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTICS -->\\n| length              = {{convert|62|km|mi|abbr=on}}\\n| width_min           = \\n| width_avg           = \\n| width_max           = \\n| depth_min           = \\n| depth_avg           = \\n| depth_max           = \\n| discharge1_location = \\n| discharge1_min      = \\n| discharge1_avg      = \\n| discharge1_max      = \\n<!---------------------- BASIN FEATURES -->\\n| source1             = [[Nederrijn]]\\n| source1_location    = [[Wijk bij Duurstede]], [[Utrecht]]\\n| source1_coordinates = \\n| source1_elevation   = \\n| mouth               = [[Nieuwe Maas]]\\n| mouth_location      = [[Kinderdijk]], [[South Holland]]\\n| mouth_coordinates   = \\n| mouth_elevation     = \\n| progression         = \\n| river_system        = \\n| basin_size          = \\n| tributaries_left    = \\n| tributaries_right   = \\n| custom_label        = \\n| custom_data         = \\n| extra               = \\n}}\\n\\nThe '''Lek''' ({{IPA|nl|lɛk}}) is a [[river]] in the western [[Netherlands]] of some {{cvt|60|km}} in length.<ref>{{Cite web | url=http://encyclopedia.kids.net.au/page/le/Lek_River | title=Kids.Net.Au - Encyclopedia > Lek River | access-date=2024-05-02 | archive-date=2021-01-27 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210127202432/http://encyclopedia.kids.net.au/page/le/Lek_River | url-status=live }}</ref> It is the continuation of the [[Nederrijn]] after the [[Kromme Rijn]] branches off at the town of [[Wijk bij Duurstede]]. The main westbound [[waterway]] is hereafter called the Lek River. The Nederrijn is, itself, a [[distributary]] branch of the river [[Rhine]].\\n\\nPortions of the river form the boundary between the provinces of Utrecht and [[Gelderland]], and between Utrecht and South Holland.\\n\\nIn Roman times, the Nederrijn flowed into the Kromme Rijn and these streams were the main outflow of the river Rhine. When the Kromme Rijn began to silt up in the Middle Ages, the Lek became the primary branch. A short distance past Wijk bij Duurstede, the river intersects with the [[Amsterdam-Rhine Canal]], which continues south towards the [[Waal (river)|Waal]]. A branch of this canal, the ''Lekkanaal'' (Lek Canal), is connected to the river in the city of [[Nieuwegein]].\\n\\nOther major towns on its banks are [[Culemborg]], [[Vianen]], [[Schoonhoven]], [[Nieuw-Lekkerland]], [[Lekkerkerk]], [[Bergambacht]], and [[Krimpen aan de Lek]]. The bed of the river lies slightly higher than the surrounding lands and [[dike (construction)|dikes]] are therefore essential to contain the Lek. At the village of [[Kinderdijk]] the Lek meets the [[Noord River]] and the combined stream is thereafter known as the [[Nieuwe Maas]] as it flows down towards the [[North Sea]].\\n\\n<!-- Deleted image removed: [[Image:RMSDeltaEast.jpg|thumb|250px|none|Satellite image of the eastern part of the Rhine-Meuse delta showing river Lek (e) &mdash; the [[Kromme Rijn]] stream is too small to show up on this picture.]] -->\"}}",
